## 5. Payment adapter and immutable ledger

Do not hard-code Whish or OMT throughout the application.

Use a provider adapter:

```text
PaymentProvider interface
WhishAdapter
OMTAdapter
FutureProviderAdapter
```

The ledger should track:

```text
order_id
provider
provider_transaction_id
currency
gross_amount
provider_fee
platform_fee
merchant_amount
driver_amount
refund_amount
chargeback_amount
settlement_batch
settlement_date
status
```

Provider adapter operations should include:

```text
create payment link
verify payment
handle webhook
refund
partial refund
reconcile settlement
```

Rules:

- payment status must come from a provider-authoritative response or verified webhook;
- the server must verify amount and currency;
- every provider event must be idempotent;
- USD and LBP remain separate currencies;
- refunds must create ledger events;
- settlement reports must reconcile against order records;
- split payments remain disabled until provider and Lebanese legal approval.

**Recommendation:** Essential before scaling prepaid and diaspora orders.

