# P1 — Add for better delivery and customer experience

## 6. Road-aware routing and ETA

Straight-line distance is not enough for Lebanon.

Use one routing provider for:

- driving distance;
- road-aware ETA;
- mountain routes;
- village-to-village travel time;
- driver navigation;
- delivery-fee calculation;
- route risk and route feasibility.

Possible providers:

```text
Google Routes API
Mapbox Directions
OpenRouteService
```

Start with one provider. Do not run multiple routing APIs until you have measured their accuracy.

Test real routes across:

- Chouf;
- Aley;
- Baabda;
- Metn;
- Keserwan;
- Beirut;
- Bekaa;
- North Lebanon;
- South Lebanon.

Maintain an internal route matrix for important village pairs because generic routing estimates may be poor on mountain roads.

**Recommendation:** Add road-aware routing before expanding delivery zones.

---

## 7. Address and landmark intelligence

Lebanese deliveries often depend on villages, landmarks, buildings, floors, local directions, and dropped pins rather than standardized street addresses.

Store structured address data:

```text
village
neighborhood
landmark
building
floor
phone contact
map pin
delivery instructions
Arabic version
English version
```

Use AI to normalize text, but never let AI decide whether a location is deliverable.

Support:

- dropped location pins;
- “near [landmark]” directions;
- voice-note instructions;
- driver correction feedback;
- saved addresses;
- customer callback;
- Arabic and English address summaries.

**Recommendation:** This may improve successful delivery more than adding another AI model.

