# P1 — Improve AI quality

## 9. Use a model router

Do not send every message to the most expensive or most capable model.

Recommended routing:

```text
Deterministic code:
buttons, menus, cart changes, order status, STOP, privacy commands

Fast/low-cost model:
intent classification, typo correction, Arabizi normalization, simple search

Structured vision model:
menu extraction, item/price candidates, image understanding

Claude:
complex complaints, ambiguous requests, difficult support, menu reasoning

OpenAI or selected structured model:
extraction, embeddings, classification, or validated voice/vision workflows
```

Record:

```text
model_used
provider
prompt_version
tool_version
latency_ms
input_tokens
output_tokens
estimated_cost
success_or_failure
human_handoff
```

Use Claude and OpenAI as complementary systems. Do not call both models for every message unless an evaluation proves the benefit is worth the cost and latency.

**Recommendation:** Implement a model router after the deterministic order flow is reliable.

