# P2 — Add after operational proof

## 14. Feature flags and experimentation

Add feature flags for:

```text
recommendations
new checkout
campaigns
payment providers
new delivery fees
zone activation
voice ordering
new AI model
new merchant notification path
```

Possible tools:

```text
PostHog feature flags
Statsig
LaunchDarkly
Supabase feature_flags table
```

Start with PostHog feature flags or a small Supabase table. Avoid LaunchDarkly until the team and release complexity justify it.

---

## 15. Data warehouse

When Postgres analytics become slow or insufficient, consider:

```text
BigQuery
ClickHouse
Snowflake
```

Do not add a warehouse immediately. Start with PostHog, reporting views, and carefully designed operational metrics.

---

## 16. Kitchen printer or kitchen display system

For larger restaurants, add:

- thermal-printer integration;
- kitchen display system;
- preparation-time tracking;
- station routing;
- order sound;
- ready-for-pickup workflow.

Do not require this for every merchant on day one. WhatsApp plus the merchant portal is sufficient for the initial pilot.

---

## 17. Loyalty and referrals

Eventually add:

- points ledger;
- referral codes;
- referral fraud protection;
- restaurant-funded rewards;
- delivery-credit rewards;
- campaign attribution;
- expiry rules;
- abuse limits.

Never store loyalty balance as one editable number. Use an append-only points ledger:

```text
loyalty_account
loyalty_ledger_entries
reward_rules
reward_redemptions
referral_events
fraud_flags
```

